<http://data.silknow.org/event/0e17d20b-bc19-31df-9a37-c525fd3f528a>
        a                              ecrm:E8_Acquisition ;
        rdfs:comment                   "This pair of trousers was made in Lingga for a Malay Prince. It was presented by Cursetjee Frommurze, Esq. who was a well-known Parsi merchant in Singapore. He entered a business partnership with John Little in 1845 to form Little, Cursetjee &amp; Co., the oldest department store in Singapore. He later married to an English woman, Maryanne in 1862."@en ;
        ecrm:P22_transferred_title_to  <http://data.silknow.org/actor/f0577f91-f887-3019-bf88-f9e5ba019390> ;
        ecrm:P24_transferred_title_of  <http://data.silknow.org/object/1a02836e-5828-3561-b0b5-a5f9581bdbad> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "This pair of trousers was made in Lingga for a Malay Prince. It was presented by Cursetjee Frommurze, Esq. who was a well-known Parsi merchant in Singapore. He entered a business partnership with John Little in 1845 to form Little, Cursetjee &amp; Co., the oldest department store in Singapore. He later married to an English woman, Maryanne in 1862."@en .

